From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd9320: fixes from the audio review

From the code review of the audio patches (docs/review.md, audio pass):

- The SLIMbus port interrupt skipped ports whose interrupt was disabled,
  as wcd9335 does. Its own overflow branch disables the port, so the
  port-closed event at the end of a stream was dropped and every close
  waited out its timeout. taiko_slimbus_irq() has no such skip.
- The platform probe deferred only until the slim drvdata existed; the
  interface regmap arrives later, from the status callback. Wait for it.
- Component remove now waits for a running interrupt thread before the
  private data it uses is freed.
- The slim status callback acted on every status and redid all of its
  setup each time: on DOWN it talked to a dead bus, and on the UP after
  an ADSP restart (every boot here) it leaked a regmap and requested the
  interrupt again. It now acts on UP, sets up once, re-queries only the
  interface device's address after a restart, requests the interrupt
  only once the regmap its handler reads exists, and reports failure.
- "SLIM RXn MUX" moved a port to a second AIF by linking it onto that
  AIF's list while it was still on the first, and every RX mux read back
  whatever value was written last to any of them. The port is moved now,
  and each mux reads back its own AIF.

